 "why": "Alt text for images the approved design ships with none.\n\nDerived ONLY for award and certificate badges, the one filename family on this site that genuinely names its subject: 'World-Luxury-Spa-Awards-2024-300x300.png' IS the award, so the derivation is a fact, not a guess. Curated by hand where a filename cannot describe the image - written from the image itself or from the caption printed beside it on the page.\n\nEverything else is deliberately left alone. Machine-reading the other filenames produces 'Video', 'Doc cons', 'Eye2', 'AHV About 698image' - text that would be read aloud to a screen-reader user and indexed by Google, and worse than the empty alt it replaces. Those images are listed in image-alt-unresolved.json for a person to look at.\n\nOrnament (leaves, borders, corner flowers, the lotus mark) keeps empty alt, which is the correct value for decoration - see image-alt-decorative.json.",
